export const abstract = [
  'Managing money is a daily problem for students, young professionals and households in Pakistan. Personal spending is usually tracked in notebooks or not at all, and shared costs on trips or in shared flats lead to long chains of small, confusing repayments. Widely used tools are either designed for foreign markets, keep key features behind paid plans, or treat personal finance and group splitting as two separate products.',
  'This project presents **SmartSplit & ExpenseAI**, a full-stack web application that combines both needs in one account. The personal workspace records income and expenses in Pakistani rupees, applies monthly category budgets, generates recurring bills automatically, and reads printed receipts using a vision language model, with Tesseract.js as an offline fallback. Every extracted line is verified by the user in a human-in-the-loop dialog before it is saved, and verified items are compared against a price book of 100 grocery products to suggest cheaper alternatives. A background job refreshes the price book every morning from five online Pakistani stores, reading only what each store\'s robots.txt permits and keeping a store\'s previous prices whenever it cannot be read. Savings goals show how much has been put aside, whether the user is on pace, and how much to save each month, and a zakat calculator compares the user\'s net wealth with the nisab using gold and silver prices fetched automatically. The group workspace supports multi-payer expenses, four split methods (equal, exact, percentage and line item), a trip currency in which new expenses start, expenses entered in foreign currencies on trips abroad and converted to rupees at daily exchange rates, and a settlement engine based on the greedy Min-Cash-Flow algorithm, which guarantees that a group of V members is settled in at most V − 1 payments.',
  'The system is built on the MERN stack (MongoDB, Express, React and Node.js) and exposes 84 REST endpoints. Money is stored as integer rupees, balances are always recomputed from expenses by database aggregation, and every group request is authorised on the server. Authentication uses short-lived JSON Web Tokens with rotating refresh tokens and Google OAuth 2.0, and email can be sent through the Gmail API where the hosting provider blocks SMTP. The implementation is verified by 319 automated unit, API and property-based tests, all passing, and is deployed publicly with every change tested before it goes live. On the demonstration trip of five members and seven expenses, the settlement engine reduced 20 naive pairwise debts to 4 payments.',
];
export const keywords = 'expense management, debt simplification, Min-Cash-Flow, greedy algorithm, receipt OCR, vision language model, multi-currency, savings goals, zakat, web scraping, robots.txt, MERN stack, JWT';

